-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Scooby Doo in the Castle Mystery
  Publisher   Elite, 1986
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Scooby Doo in the Castle Mystery (1986)(Elite Systems).z80
  MD5         8a82e06f6829a2a1c30781491cfbc42e

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

  Memory      Any Next: a 1MB Next has the memory for the game. Enhanced needs
              a 1MB Next, and is not offered on a smaller one.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  The default keeps the original look, and the small colour clash the original
  has stays (see the note). The patch adds the menu, its cheats and the Next
  start-up. Game logic is unchanged. Enhanced colours, an option on the menu,
  are below.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    The Spec256 set's colours as they are, for the play window only:
              scenery, figures and the player in its 256 colours over the
              set's background colour. The set's picture, not this release's
              attributes, gives every colour. Source: Enhanced colours:
              Armando Quaranta (Spec256).

  Pace        original

  Changes     1.0: the original game with Sinclair's 48K ROM as the whole alt
              ROM, no game byte changed and no hook in the default; the tape's
              loading screen; Enhanced: the play window in the Spec256 colours
              on a double-buffered Layer 2, off by default; five tested cheats

  Note        Keys: ENTER starts, J then K Kempston (or I, C), K keyboard, P
              practice; X right, Z left, O up, K down, P punch, U pause, Y
              quits. Default: the original game, picture and all, no hook.
              Enhanced, on the menu, off by default: the play window in the
              Spec256 set's colours on Layer 2, every figure in its own
              colours, so no clash there. The 48K game, beeper sound; fits a
              1MB Next. Known issues: default keeps the original's small clash
              (0.35%, 0.13%, 0.08% of figure cells in levels 1-3, 3.6% in
              level 4 rooms); Enhanced pace in JNext against the original, 12
              runs of 800 updates in lockstep: whole -0.95 to -0.00%, quiet
              thirds -0.04 to +0.11%, busy thirds -2.84 to -0.05%, slowest 20
              updates up to +2.80%; the No ghosts and No enemies cheats lost a
              life in some test runs (cause not established). Missing: in
              Enhanced the panel, title and menus stay in the original colours
              (the set paints the panel too); natural play to the end (later
              levels by a test poke); hardware untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Immune to nasties
   3  No ghosts
   4  No enemies
   5  Invincibility

  The archive's POKEs for this release, tested in the simulator with the same
  keys with and without each: Infinite lives and Invincibility (lives never
  fall), Immune to nasties (one life lost in one seed of three), No ghosts and
  No enemies (no enemy drawn; a life lost in one or two seeds of three; cause
  not established). Left out: Lives (asks a value); Immunity but you die on a
  bad jump (29479: it opens LD BC,nn / LD (HL),E, writing a byte through HL
  every update); Ghosts only (no clear result).

